<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahipala I (Gurjara-Pratihara)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-i-pratihara">Mahipala I</a> was king of the Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> in the early 10th century. Around 916 the Rashtrakuta king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indra-iii">Indra III</a> invaded and sacked Kannauj, but Mahipala recovered his capital, apparently with help from the Chandela king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>. His court poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajashekhara">Rajashekhara</a> praised him, but the empire's decline set in during his reign.</p></div>
